Whole books, graduate courses and a sustained thermal programme (@th-programme: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Engineering-Thermodynamics-Yan.lingua#r_6AX93SRMGE0XXJTQ1NW6X9QXTW", #source "../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ", #source "../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1", #source "../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD", #source "../sources/Termodinamica-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0ABCKSRZBN8T4Y4FV1FQPWNY4Z", #source "../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC", #source "../sources/Nano-to-Macro-Transport-MIT-2-57.lingua#r_1YF7TD689ZRGQ51D4B3NGVHZQG", #source "../sources/Radiative-Transfer-MIT-2-58J.lingua#r_0SGHEYZJFKN0ZNS3AYJ39XPT86", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../research/Advanced-thermal-investigations.lingua#r_2138JZQJ9QSATXRKZKMY05SV6P") { r_7NHTEAK764F0WSPPZNHZB7CJ1M
**Read:** [Introduction to Engineering Thermodynamics — Claire Yu Yan](../sources/Introduction-to-Engineering-Thermodynamics-Yan.lingua#r_6AX93SRMGE0XXJTQ1NW6X9QXTW), the whole book; [Engineering Thermodynamics — Olivier Cleynen](../sources/Engineering-Thermodynamics-Cleynen.lingua#r_38CM7HKS0GSN5T09YDXFKHRVGQ), the whole book; [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), the whole book; [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), the whole book; [Termodinâmica — Bernhard Lesche, UFJF](../sources/Termodinamica-Lesche-UFJF.lingua#r_0ABCKSRZBN8T4Y4FV1FQPWNY4Z), all available relevant chapters; [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC), the full public course; [Nano-to-Macro Transport Processes — MIT 2.57](../sources/Nano-to-Macro-Transport-MIT-2-57.lingua#r_1YF7TD689ZRGQ51D4B3NGVHZQG), the full public course; [Radiative Transfer — MIT 2.58J](../sources/Radiative-Transfer-MIT-2-58J.lingua#r_0SGHEYZJFKN0ZNS3AYJ39XPT86), the full available course.

Begin with all six Yan chapters and substantial independent problems. Read the whole Cleynen book as the engineering development; use the complete available Lesche notes as a Portuguese companion. Work the full mathematical units needed for the derivations instead of skipping an unfamiliar operation. The earlier quantitative, chemistry and measurement Records are available at each point of use.

Then study all of DeVoe and all of Lienhard, including appendices where used, derivations, solved examples and substantial unseen exercises from every major subject. Follow the full MIT 2.51 reading sequence and the complete Vedula analytical course. Work the full focused Das convection course; the available UFSC convection/numerical courses provide a Portuguese graduate companion with a different emphasis.

For advanced depth, complete the public MIT 2.43 thermodynamics programme, MIT 2.58J radiative-transfer material and MIT 2.57 nano-to-macro programme. Distinguish public files from missing lectures or separately published readings. Work the actual assignments and explanatory examinations where supplied. Read complete primary property releases and methods papers when a calculation or investigation depends on them.

Finish [Explain a thermal system before choosing a formula](Explain-a-thermal-system-before-choosing-a-formula.lingua#r_07WVS4C6WEPKYQJ1TE7K6R72E8) and [Derive and check a combined transport model](Derive-and-check-a-combined-transport-model.lingua#r_77N3EXRST6J39D13QJ83RDY9VJ), the four inspectable examples, and advanced investigations in each of six groups: equilibrium/properties/cycles; analytical/numerical conduction; convection/phase change/exchangers; radiation; measurement/inverse methods; microscopic/coupled transport. Read all of the chosen studies' primary sources, not just their abstracts. Add the performed physical investigation for practical completion, an integrated service and an independent research/revision cycle. The advanced study links give choices within this substantial programme; they are ordinary Records, not enrolment gates.

**Continue:** [Advanced thermal investigations](../research/Advanced-thermal-investigations.lingua#r_2138JZQJ9QSATXRKZKMY05SV6P).

**Return:** [Thermodynamics and heat transfer](../Thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer.lingua#r_6KQBZNJM6WNV9A69R3DZY1NH7E).
